#. Short description.
#, gp-priority: high
msgid "Membership register, volunteer hours and a fair membership fee: members who volunteer more pay less. Optional discount and Stripe payments."
msgstr "Membership register, volunteer hours and a fair membership fee: members who volunteer more pay less. Optional discount and Stripe payments."

#. Plugin name.
#, gp-priority: high
msgid "Fair Member Fees"
msgstr "Fair Member Fees"

#. Found in faq paragraph.
msgid "Nothing, unless you turn on \"Delete data\" in the settings."
msgstr "Nothing, unless you turn on \"Delete data\" in the settings."

#. Found in faq paragraph.
msgid "No. The server always calculates the fee from the saved block settings and the recorded hours."
msgstr "No. The server always calculates the fee from the saved block settings and the recorded hours."

#. Found in faq paragraph.
msgid "Only administrators and editors (the capability <code>famefe_manage</code>)."
msgstr "Only administrators and editors (the capability <code>famefe_manage</code>)."

#. Found in faq paragraph.
msgid "Every logged-in member records own hours. Administrators and editors can record hours for any member. In the settings you can allow logged-in non-members to record hours too; their hours count only in the totals."
msgstr "Every logged-in member records own hours. Administrators and editors can record hours for any member. In the settings you can allow logged-in non-members to record hours too; their hours count only in the totals."

#. Found in faq paragraph.
msgid "The button is off until you turn it on in the Membership fees block (\"Payment button\"). Turn it on once the volunteer hours of the period are closed and the fees are final; until then members see the fee calculated from the hours recorded so far. Online payment also needs the Stripe keys in the settings. If your club only keeps records of hours, simply leave the button off."
msgstr "The button is off until you turn it on in the Membership fees block (\"Payment button\"). Turn it on once the volunteer hours of the period are closed and the fees are final; until then members see the fee calculated from the hours recorded so far. Online payment also needs the Stripe keys in the settings. If your club only keeps records of hours, simply leave the button off."

#. Found in faq header.
msgid "What happens with the data when I delete the plugin?"
msgstr "What happens with the data when I delete the plugin?"

#. Found in faq header.
msgid "Can the amount to pay be changed in the browser?"
msgstr "Can the amount to pay be changed in the browser?"

#. Found in faq header.
msgid "Who sees the form for cash payments?"
msgstr "Who sees the form for cash payments?"

#. Found in faq header.
msgid "Who can record hours?"
msgstr "Who can record hours?"

#. Found in faq header.
msgid "Why do members not see the payment button?"
msgstr "Why do members not see the payment button?"

#. Found in installation list item.
msgid "Add the blocks to your pages (search for \"Fair Member Fees\" in the block inserter). Set the period, the base fee and the discount in the Membership fees block."
msgstr "Add the blocks to your pages (search for \"Fair Member Fees\" in the block inserter). Set the period, the base fee and the discount in the Membership fees block."

#. Found in installation list item.
msgid "In <strong>Member Fees → Settings</strong> set the currency and, for online payments, your Stripe keys and the webhook."
msgstr "In <strong>Member Fees → Settings</strong> set the currency and, for online payments, your Stripe keys and the webhook."

#. Found in installation list item.
msgid "Go to <strong>Member Fees → Members</strong> and add your members; link them to their user accounts so that they can record hours and pay online."
msgstr "Go to <strong>Member Fees → Members</strong> and add your members; link them to their user accounts so that they can record hours and pay online."

#. Found in installation list item.
msgid "Install and activate the plugin."
msgstr "Install and activate the plugin."

#. Found in description paragraph.
msgid "The editor scripts in <code>build/</code> are compiled from the human-readable sources in <code>src/</code> (included in the plugin) with <code>@wordpress/scripts</code> (<code>npm install</code>, <code>npm run build</code>). The development repository is public: https://github.com/globus2008/fair-member-fees"
msgstr "The editor scripts in <code>build/</code> are compiled from the human-readable sources in <code>src/</code> (included in the plugin) with <code>@wordpress/scripts</code> (<code>npm install</code>, <code>npm run build</code>). The development repository is public: https://github.com/globus2008/fair-member-fees"

#. Found in description paragraph.
msgid "Stripe terms of service: https://stripe.com/legal/ssa – Stripe privacy policy: https://stripe.com/privacy"
msgstr "Stripe terms of service: https://stripe.com/legal/ssa – Stripe privacy policy: https://stripe.com/privacy"

#. Found in description paragraph.
msgid "This plugin connects to <strong>Stripe</strong> (https://stripe.com) to let members pay their membership fee by card. It is used only when you enter a Stripe secret key in the plugin settings."
msgstr "This plugin connects to <strong>Stripe</strong> (https://stripe.com) to let members pay their membership fee by card. It is used only when you enter a Stripe secret key in the plugin settings."

#. Found in description paragraph.
msgid "Instead of the percentage, you can set the total to collect: the discount of the same members is then calculated so that all regular members pay exactly this amount together (for example to give back what the double fees of members without hours brought above the expected total)."
msgstr "Instead of the percentage, you can set the total to collect: the discount of the same members is then calculated so that all regular members pay exactly this amount together (for example to give back what the double fees of members without hours brought above the expected total)."

#. Found in description paragraph.
msgid "Set a share of members (e.g. 60 %) and a discount (e.g. 20 %) in the Membership fees block: the given share of regular members with the lowest fees pays the given percentage less. Members with the same fee as the last of them get it too; members without hours never get it. The discount is not added to the fees of the others."
msgstr "Set a share of members (e.g. 60 %) and a discount (e.g. 20 %) in the Membership fees block: the given share of regular members with the lowest fees pays the given percentage less. Members with the same fee as the last of them get it too; members without hours never get it. The discount is not added to the fees of the others."

#. Found in description paragraph.
msgid "<strong>Discount (optional)</strong>"
msgstr "<strong>Discount (optional)</strong>"

#. Found in description paragraph.
msgid "Whoever does not volunteer pays twice the base fee, so paying instead of working is never the cheaper choice. Hours of honorary members and non-members are shown in the totals but do not change the fees."
msgstr "Whoever does not volunteer pays twice the base fee, so paying instead of working is never the cheaper choice. Hours of honorary members and non-members are shown in the totals but do not change the fees."

#. Found in description paragraph.
msgid "<strong>How the fee is calculated</strong>"
msgstr "<strong>How the fee is calculated</strong>"

#. Found in description paragraph.
msgid "<strong>Features</strong>"
msgstr "<strong>Features</strong>"

#. Found in description paragraph.
msgid "Clubs live from the work of their members. Fair Member Fees rewards it: every member records the hours they volunteered, and the membership fee of each member is calculated from them. Whoever works for the club pays less; whoever does not, pays twice the base fee – paying instead of working is never the cheaper choice."
msgstr "Clubs live from the work of their members. Fair Member Fees rewards it: every member records the hours they volunteered, and the membership fee of each member is calculated from them. Whoever works for the club pays less; whoever does not, pays twice the base fee – paying instead of working is never the cheaper choice."

#. Found in description list item.
msgid "When the member returns, the plugin asks Stripe whether the payment was completed. Stripe also sends the result to the webhook address of the plugin."
msgstr "When the member returns, the plugin asks Stripe whether the payment was completed. Stripe also sends the result to the webhook address of the plugin."

#. Found in description list item.
msgid "When a member clicks the payment button, the plugin sends to Stripe: the amount and currency, the name of the payment (\"Membership fee\" and the period), the member's e-mail address, the member ID and the period, and the addresses of your page to return to. The member then enters the card details directly on the Stripe payment page."
msgstr "When a member clicks the payment button, the plugin sends to Stripe: the amount and currency, the name of the payment (\"Membership fee\" and the period), the member's email address, the member ID and the period, and the addresses of your page to return to. The member then enters the card details directly on the Stripe payment page."

#. Found in description list item.
msgid "A member without any recorded hours in the period always pays twice the base fee."
msgstr "A member without any recorded hours in the period always pays twice the base fee."

#. Found in description list item.
msgid "The unreduced fees add up to more than the expected total; the difference is taken off every fee equally. No fee goes below zero (the rest is shared by the others)."
msgstr "The unreduced fees add up to more than the expected total; the difference is taken off every fee equally. No fee goes below zero (the rest is shared by the others)."

#. Found in description list item.
msgid "Unreduced fee = expected total × (1 − share of hours)."
msgstr "Unreduced fee = expected total × (1 − share of hours)."

#. Found in description list item.
msgid "Share of hours = hours of the member / hours of all regular members."
msgstr "Share of hours = hours of the member / hours of all regular members."

#. Found in description list item.
msgid "Expected total = base fee × number of regular members."
msgstr "Expected total = base fee × number of regular members."

#. Found in description list item.
msgid "Ready for translation."
msgstr "Ready for translation."

#. Found in description list item.
msgid "<strong>Fee calculation explained</strong> – the method on an example with your own numbers."
msgstr "<strong>Fee calculation explained</strong> – the method on an example with your own numbers."

#. Found in description list item.
msgid "<strong>Members list</strong>,"
msgstr "<strong>Members list</strong>,"

